From 31f30d7cacf9f7a7b218ec6a9c3861cc8614e67f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: airidosas252 <airidaslideikis@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 14:06:20 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 27/28] ir3: add ray_stack_ir3 and reserve its state block

ray_stack keeps its traversal state in 12 full registers that the
hardware shares across the wave, lane i's dword d in register
base + (12 * i + d) / 64. RA can't treat that as a value: a copy under a
divergent mask only moves the active lanes' columns, and RA moves and
splits live ranges freely.

So for shaders that use ray_stack, RA's full register limit is lowered
by 12 registers, and after RA the block goes right above the highest
register in use and is written into every ray_stack. Nothing after RA
allocates registers, and the footprint and wave count include the
block. Other shaders are unchanged.

The instruction is kept like a store even when its result is unused
(the reset), is ordered like a ballot, and is synced with (ss). The
block is sized for wave64, which is all a8xx runs. Gated by a new
has_ray_stack prop, set for a8xx only.
